description:
**File:** rust/lichen-rpl/src/multi_instance.rs
**Lines:** 590-592 (queue_for_propagation)

**Issue:** Unlike peers (MAX_PEERS=64), candidates (MAX_CANDIDATES=32), and received_routes (MAX_RECEIVED_ROUTE_PEERS=64), the pending propagation queue has no maximum size. A malicious or buggy caller can queue unlimited messages.

**Trigger:** Repeated calls to `queue_for_propagation()` without draining via `get_pending_propagations()`.

**Impact:** Memory exhaustion DoS. Inconsistent with other collections in this module that have documented DoS protection.

**Fix:** Add `MAX_PENDING_PROPAGATIONS` constant and return `false` when limit reached:
```rust
pub const MAX_PENDING_PROPAGATIONS: usize = 256;

pub fn queue_for_propagation(&self, message: DaoBackboneMessage) -> bool {
    let mut pending = self.pending.lock().expect("pending mutex poisoned");
    if pending.len() >= MAX_PENDING_PROPAGATIONS {
        return false;
    }
    pending.push(message);
    true
}
```
